  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is released from height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> on a smooth curved surface which ends into a vertical loop of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>, as shown. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></math>, then<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image4-b7b1532a-5cbd-466e-ac6d-af905a74b5bd.jpg\" style=\"height: 115px; width: 200px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wzRNr",
      "text": "the particle reaches the top of the loop with zero velocity",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "b9g8U",
      "text": "the particle reaches the top of the loop with a non-zero velocity",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "r4c3i",
      "text": "the particle breaks off at a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></math> from base",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sncsK",
      "text": "the particle breaks off at a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "To reach the top of loop, particle must have a minimum speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi></msqrt></math> at the bottom of the loop.<br /><br />but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;, so the block won't reach the highest point of the track.",
